<title>NORWAY: Statoil awards seismic contract.</title>
<headline>Statoil awards seismic contract.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Den norske stats oljeselskap AS said on Wednesday it has award a 150-200 million crowns contract to Geco Prakla for three-dimensional seismic surveying during 1997.</p>
<p>The work is due to start in February in the southern North Sea and will cover surveys on the Norwegian, Danish, British and Irish continental shelves.</p>
<p>The surveys will cover about 4,000 square kilometres.</p>
<p>During the summer, seismic data will be gathered using three vessels simultaneoulsy, each towing six to 10 hydrophone streamers, Statoil said.</p>
<p>Geco Prakla had a similar contract with Statoil in 1996.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
